{title: 446 - Lo, What a Glorious Sight Appears}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Early Advent}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[G]Lo, what a glorious sight appears To our believing [D7]eyes!
[D7]The earth [G]and seas are passed away, And the old rolling skies.
[D7]And the old rolling skies, [G]And the old rolling skies;
[G]The earth [D]and seas are passed away, And the old rolling skies.
[D/F#]O that will be [G]joyful, joyful, joyful!
[G]O that will [C]be joyful When we [D7]meet to part [G]no more!
[G]When we meet to part no more [D]on Canaan's happy [G]shore;
[G]'Tis there we'll meet at Jesus' feet, When we meet to part no [D7]more!

Refrain:
[D7]O that [G]will be joyful, joyful, [D]joyful!
[D]O that will be joyful
[G]When we meet [D]to part no more!
[D/F#]When we meet [G]to part no more
[G]On Canaan's [C]happy shore;
[D7]'Tis there we'll meet [G]at Jesus' feet,
[D]When we meet to part no more!

Verse 2:
[G]Attending angels shout for joy
[D7]And [G]the bright armies sing-
[D7]Mortals! Behold [G]the sacred seat
[G]Of [D]your descending [G]King.
[D/F#]Of your [G]descending King,
[G]Of your [C]descending [G]King;
[G]Mortals! Behold [D]the sacred [G]seat
[G]Of your descending King.

Verse 3:
[G]His own soft hand shall wipe the tears
[D7]From [G]every weeping eye;
[D7]And pains, and groans, [G]and griefs, and fears,
[G]And [D]death itself shall [G]die!
[D/F#]And death [G]itself shall die,
[G]And death [C]itself [D7]shall [G]die;
[G]And pains, and groans, and [D]griefs, and [G]fears,
[G]And death itself shall die.

Verse 4:
[G]How long, dear Savior! Oh, how long
[D7]Shall [G]this bright hour delay?
[D7]Fly swifter round, [G]ye wheels of time!
[G]And [D]bring the welcome [G]day.
[D/F#]And bring [G]the welcome day,
[G]And bring [C]the welcome [G]day;
[G]Fly swifter round, ye [D]wheels of [G]time!
[G]And bring the welcome day.
